# Barrio Logan Guest Concierge — environment variables
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW TO USE
#   Local dev:  cp .env.example .env.local  →  fill in values  →  npm run dev
#   Production: set these as DEPLOYMENT SECRETS in Vercel / Cloudflare (not in a file).
#
# NEVER commit .env.local or a real API key to the repo.
# .env.local is (and must stay) in .gitignore.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- Model provider selection -----------------------------------------
# Controls which AI backend /api/chat uses.
#   "ollama"     → local open-weight model via Ollama (default for dev)
#   "anthropic"  → Claude Haiku via Anthropic API (recommended for prod)
#
# To swap dev → prod: change this one variable in your deployment secrets.
# Zero code changes required.
MODEL_PROVIDER=ollama

# ---- Ollama (dev only) ------------------------------------------------
# Only used when MODEL_PROVIDER=ollama.
# Make sure Ollama is running locally: https://ollama.com/download
#
# Base URL of your local Ollama server (default shown below).
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
#
# Model name — must be pulled first: `ollama pull llama3.2`
# Lightweight options: llama3.2 (~2 GB), phi3 (~2 GB), mistral (~4 GB)
OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2

# ---- Anthropic / Claude Haiku (production) ----------------------------
# Only used when MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic.
#
# SECURITY: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is a SERVER SECRET.
#   • Never commit it to the repo.
#   • Never reference it in any client component — it is read only inside
#     the server-side /api/chat route handler.
#   • Set it exclusively via your host's secret manager:
#       Vercel  → Project Settings → Environment Variables → add as "Secret"
#       Cloudflare → wrangler secret put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#   • The @ai-sdk/anthropic package reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY automatically
#     from process.env; no code change is needed.
#
# Uncomment these lines as a REMINDER of what to set — fill in the real
# key only inside your host's secret UI, never in this file.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...          ← SET AS A DEPLOYMENT SECRET, not here
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5     ← optional override; default is claude-haiku-4-5
